---
// Your Instructors band (Task 7, Course PDP Chunk A) — Figma desktop
// 1007:7830 (file FX7PDNvhZwyozODaq8Q8i7) / mobile 1109:14383 (the "Sole
// Switch Pro Page" > "Your Instructors" instance inside the
// professional-courses mobile frame 1109:14374). Prop is `{ item }` (same
// shape as CourseOverview/YoullStopAndInstead/ComparisonChart/Testimonial),
// reading `item.pdp.instructors`. Deliberately generic — nothing
// course-specific is hardcoded — so it can also serve the deferred Walk
// product PDP later without changes.
//
// `item.pdp.instructors` = an array of `{ photo, name, credential, bio }`,
// this task's brief-mandated shape, one entry per instructor card. Both
// pulled frames show the identical 2 instructors, same content on desktop
// and mobile — no disagreement to flag here, unlike CourseOverview's
// `details`/Audience conflict.
//
// `credential` is a slight misnomer against what the frame actually shows:
// the styled teal line under each name reads a LOCATION ("Lakewood,
// Colorado" / "Salem, Massachusetts"), not a professional credential —
// actual credentials live inline in `name` itself (the "Dr." honorific,
// the "DPT" suffix on Riley's). Populated per the brief's exact field name
// anyway (same "keep the brief's shape, document the reality" precedent
// Testimonial.astro's near-always-null `role` field sets) rather than
// renaming the field to `location` and drifting from the brief's contract.
//
// `bio` is an array of paragraph strings — one per real `<p>` in the pulled
// Figma code, same convention Testimonial.astro's `quote` field uses.
// Conley's bio is a genuine 4-paragraph biography; Riley's is a single
// paragraph — both frames agree on both bios verbatim.
//
// ---- Photo ---------------------------------------------------------------
// No dedicated instructor photography exists (this course has never had a
// PDP before; catalog.js's `instructorsByline` comment already flags this —
// "the 2 avatar circles are flat placeholders" — as this task's job to
// address). `photo` reuses the same PLP course shot every other image slot
// on this page already reuses (see catalog.js's `overview`/`features`
// comments), rendered in a circular crop box (overflow:hidden + object-fit:
// cover — same placeholder-media idiom CourseOverview/FourColumn use,
// `border-radius:50%` added for Figma's circular mask, `--color-border`
// background while the image loads — see InstructorCard.astro). `alt=""` —
// decorative: the placeholder is a generic product shot, not an actual
// likeness of the named instructor, so a name-echoing alt (e.g. "Dr.
// Courtney Conley") would misrepresent the image rather than describe it;
// once real headshots replace this placeholder, that alt should become the
// instructor's name.
//
// ---- Heading semantics -----------------------------------------------
// The section heading is a real `<h2>` (sibling to CourseOverview's/
// ComparisonChart's own `<h2>`s). Each instructor name (InstructorCard.astro)
// is a real `<h3>` — Figma binds it to the SAME 32px `text-h3` style as the
// section heading (visual sizing only), but semantically it's one level
// down, keeping this page's h1 hero -> h2 sections -> h3 names outline
// correct rather than mirroring Figma's shared style name into a duplicate
// `<h2>`.
//
// `item.pdp.instructorsHeading` is an optional per-item override of the
// heading text, defaulting to every course's existing "Your Instructors" —
// the same "optional field, existing content is the default" idiom
// FourColumn.astro's `item.pdp.featuresHeading` already establishes (the
// closest precedent: a section whose heading varies per item). Added
// because Walk — the first PRODUCT to render this section (see file header)
// — is a book, so its own Figma heading (BOTH breakpoints, node
// `I721:7907;173:318` desktop / `I1017:9594;183:393` mobile) reads "Meet the
// Authors", not "Your Instructors" (its 2 cards are the book's authors, not
// course instructors). Every course keeps rendering the unmodified default
// by simply never setting this field — confirmed byte-identical via this
// branch's regression diff.
//
// ---- "Read More" bio toggle --------------------------------------------
// Both frames show every bio visually truncated (a fixed-height box, ending
// mid-sentence with "…") with a real "Read More" button + chevron below it.
// Unlike Testimonial.astro's prev/next arrows (built as inert decoration
// because there's nothing to page between with only one testimonial in the
// data), the full bio text for BOTH instructors is already present in the
// pulled Figma data here, so there's a real "more" to reveal. A working
// toggle costs nothing extra and avoids shipping a button that visibly does
// nothing — see InstructorCard.astro for the toggle markup (CSS line-clamp
// + a real `<button aria-expanded>`); the delegated click listener below is
// the same event-delegation idiom ProductDetails.astro's buy box uses.
// Figma only designed the COLLAPSED state; the expanded state's "Read Less"
// label + 90°-rotated chevron are this component's own reasonable
// counterpart to a real toggle, not a literal Figma pull. This repo's other
// interactive PDP controls (e.g. ProductDetails' Add to Cart) already
// assume JS is available; this toggle makes the same assumption, no
// `<noscript>` fallback.
//
// ---- Layout / tokens -------------------------------------------------
// Desktop (1007:7830): a centered flex row (`flex-wrap`, `justify-content:
// center`, --space-8 gap) of fixed-384px-wide cards. Mobile (1109:14383):
// the same cards stacked full-width (capped at the same 384px so they don't
// stretch past it on a wider mobile viewport) — reproduced as a single
// mobile-first column layout, switched to a wrapped row at
// `min-width: 1024px`, rather than duplicating markup per breakpoint. Both
// the 384px card cap and InstructorCard.astro's 222px circular photo are
// literals measured directly off the frames (no dedicated token for
// either) — same "literal px value, flagged inline" allowance every
// sibling section here takes. Every other spacing value in both frames (the
// 48/64/32/24/16/8px gaps and paddings) maps onto an exact --space token,
// used unmodified below.
//
// Name = --type-h3 (600/32) at both breakpoints even though mobile's own
// pulled code shows 24px — same "one non-responsive h3 token" precedent
// CourseOverview.astro's own heading sets. Credential/location = --type-h4
// (500/24), same precedent (mobile's pulled code shows 20px); Figma's own
// color binding for it, `var(--text-inverse,#047791)`, is an oddly-named
// variable but its hex is an EXACT match to `--color-teal`, so no literal
// is needed despite the confusing token name. Bio = --type-body-sm (400/14),
// an exact match. Toggle button text = --type-cta (600/16), an exact match
// to Figma's SemiBold/16 "cta" text style.
import InstructorCard from './InstructorCard.astro';

const { item } = Astro.props;
const instructors = item.pdp?.instructors ?? [];
const heading = item.pdp?.instructorsHeading ?? 'Your Instructors';
---
{instructors.length > 0 && (
  <section class="your-instructors" data-pdp-id={item.id}>
    <div class="your-instructors__inner">
      <h2 class="your-instructors__heading">{heading}</h2>
      <div class="your-instructors__row">
        {instructors.map((instructor) => (
          <InstructorCard instructor={instructor} />
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}
<style>
  .your-instructors__inner {
    max-width: var(--container-max);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: var(--space-5);
    padding-block: var(--space-7);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .your-instructors__heading {
    font: var(--type-h3);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    text-align: center;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .your-instructors__row {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    width: 100%;
  }

  /* ---- Desktop (Figma 1007:7830, ≥1024) -------------------------------- */
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .your-instructors__inner {
      padding-inline: var(--space-7);
    }
    .your-instructors__row {
      flex-direction: row;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      justify-content: center;
      gap: var(--space-8);
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Bio expand/collapse — delegated click listener at module scope (same
  // event-delegation idiom ProductDetails.astro's buy box uses). Each
  // instructor card's bio starts visually clamped (`data-collapsed` — see
  // InstructorCard.astro's styles); clicking its "Read More"/"Read Less"
  // toggle flips `aria-expanded` on the button and removes/restores the
  // `data-collapsed` attribute on that card's own bio element, found fresh
  // via the button's `aria-controls` id (never a cached reference) —
  // nothing to leak or go stale across Astro's ClientRouter swaps, and no
  // `astro:after-swap` re-init is needed either: a fresh page load already
  // renders every card collapsed by default, the same state this handler
  // resets to.
  document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const target = e.target;
    if (!(target instanceof Element)) return;
    const toggle = target.closest('[data-instructor-toggle]');
    if (!toggle) return;

    const bio = document.getElementById(toggle.getAttribute('aria-controls') ?? '');
    if (!bio) return;

    const wasExpanded = toggle.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
    toggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!wasExpanded));
    bio.toggleAttribute('data-collapsed', wasExpanded);

    const label = toggle.querySelector('[data-instructor-toggle-label]');
    if (label) label.textContent = wasExpanded ? 'Read More' : 'Read Less';
  });

  // The Read More toggle must only exist when the bio ACTUALLY overflows its
  // 4-line clamp — otherwise it is a control that reveals nothing (a false
  // affordance; same reasoning that keeps Testimonial's arrows inert when
  // there is only one quote). Overflow is WIDTH-dependent, so this cannot be
  // an authored data flag: it must be measured, and re-measured on resize.
  //
  // The listeners below are registered ONCE at module scope (Astro's
  // ClientRouter never re-executes an identical inline module), but the
  // measurement itself must re-run against each new page's DOM — hence
  // `astro:page-load`. Nodes are resolved fresh on every run; nothing is cached.
  function syncInstructorToggles() {
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-instructor-bio]').forEach((bio) => {
      const toggle = document.querySelector(`[aria-controls="${bio.id}"]`);
      if (!toggle) return;
      if (toggle.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true') return; // user opened it — leave alone
      bio.setAttribute('data-collapsed', ''); // measure the CLAMPED height
      const overflows = bio.scrollHeight > bio.clientHeight + 1; // +1 absorbs sub-pixel rounding
      toggle.hidden = !overflows;
      if (!overflows) bio.removeAttribute('data-collapsed');
    });
  }

  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', syncInstructorToggles);
  window.addEventListener('resize', () => requestAnimationFrame(syncInstructorToggles));
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', syncInstructorToggles);
  } else {
    syncInstructorToggles();
  }
</script>
